Person Re-id problem:

1- Detection:
	Given a frame, detect all people.

2- Match that person to a gallery of images in feature space.
	-> The gallery itself is extracted from running detection and getting all crops.
	
PIPELINE 01:

1- Seperare pipeline:

	-> Train detector, eg: YOLO, Faster R-CNN
	-> Run detector on images to get person crops. Note the mAP or some other metric to see how good detections are.
	-> Train Re-ID model on crops -> metric learning.
	-> At inference time, you just detect, embed and do nearest neighbour search.

PIPELINE 02:

2- Joint Training:
	
	-> The architecure is a shared backbone, Region Proposal Network, ROI, ROI align, detection head + ReID head.
	-> detection loss (bbox coord + classification) + ReID loss (triplet etc.)
	-> Joint backprop

For now we start with Pipeline 01 to get a baseline model. Today we plan to implement a detection pipeline.






PIPELINE 01 Details:

1- YOLO-Based Detection:
    1-  We use yolo to see how well the detections are. We use yolo to get the bbox prediction , confidence scores and class label. 
    2-  Once we have all the detections , we can plot a Precison-Recall Curve, the flatter it remains the better. We sort all predictions by confidence (high -> low) and we sweep through this ranked list where at each step we compute precisiona nd recall. This means that PR curve is obtianed by varying confidence threshold implicitly thorugh rnaking.
        higher recall -> low confidence region included.
        lower recall -> high confidence region only.

    3- We calculate Average Precision by ranking all the predictions according to confidence threshold, where each preiction is TP if
        -> correct class = Person
        -> IOU >= threshold
        -> matched to an unmatched gt box

        else its a FP.
    
    4- This can then be repeated at multiple levels of IoU so eg COCO style mAP@0.5:0.95 


